### Feature Resources — catálogo (JWT + RBAC)
### Un recurso es (method, path) EN PATRÓN. GET y POST sobre la misma ruta son DOS recursos.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sesion/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "admin", "password": "Admin123!" }

@token = {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### getAll — catálogo completo (103 recursos sembrados)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### getOne
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos/25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### CREATE — alta de un punto de acceso nuevo
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "GET", "path": "/api/reportes/citas/:id", "description": "Reporte de citas" }

### 409 — la tupla ya existe
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "GET", "path": "/api/propietarios", "description": "Duplicado" }

### DELETE lógico
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos/104/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### DELETE físico
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/recursos/104
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
